{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the primary uncertainty is whether a multimodal setup (combining RNA and image features) outperforms unimodal baselines, and which moderate-complexity architecture serves as a strong starting point. config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) tests the core hypothesis that fusing a learned 200-dim RNA latent (scvi_n200) with a standard CNN image embedding (resnet50) via weighted fusion, with simple average-pool aggregation across multiple profiles, yields strong validation accuracy. It avoids the most expensive choices (ViT-L, transformer aggregation) while still being a fully multimodal, multiprofile pipeline. This gives a solid performance anchor at moderate cost (estimated ~2-3x the cost of a single-modality resnet50 config, well below ViT-L + transformer configs), leaving budget for 9 further experiments to explore whether upgrading the image encoder, switching to transformer aggregation, or changing the RNA encoder yields meaningful gains."
}

